musl POSIX fnmatch
==================
Upstream: https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/
Pinned revision: 7813e9119eb5fe681b6750b8a033a0490bca0941
Source: https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/plain/src/regex/fnmatch.c?id=7813e9119eb5fe681b6750b8a033a0490bca0941
Header: https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/plain/include/fnmatch.h?id=7813e9119eb5fe681b6750b8a033a0490bca0941
License: MIT; upstream COPYRIGHT is retained verbatim. The implementation's
original author/date notice remains in src/regex/fnmatch.c.

Local changes:
- The public header is installed at compat/win32/include/fnmatch.h.
- The unused musl-private locale_impl.h include is removed.
- Conversion uses mbrtowc with a private, reset mbstate_t per character instead
  of musl's stateless mbtowc, avoiding shared conversion state in UCRT.
- Bracket conversion uses MB_CUR_MAX rather than a UTF-8-specific limit of 4.
- Tail boundaries use a forward, character-counted window for multibyte
  locales instead of UTF-8-specific backward scanning, allowing UCRT code
  pages as well. The single-byte fast path does not need extra decoding.

The matcher retains POSIX flags=0 behavior: wildcards can cross separators,
leading dots are ordinary, matching is case-sensitive, and backslash escapes
pattern characters (it is not treated as a Windows separator in patterns).
It also retains the upstream FNM_PATHNAME, FNM_NOESCAPE, FNM_PERIOD,
FNM_LEADING_DIR, and FNM_CASEFOLD flags. Multibyte conversion/classification
follows the active UCRT locale without changing the process locale.

Compile compat/win32/fnmatch.c, which includes the vendored implementation,
with /Icompat/win32/include. Do not compile src/regex/fnmatch.c separately.
No external libraries or generated files are required.
